    "'''Notes for the graphing: \n",
    "- I've written a simple graphData container class to store data about a specific graph.\n",
    "- This data includes: title, x_data (plot on x_axis / size of tree), logged_x_data (for a log graph), y_data (for the y_axis / time),\n",
    "summary_text: a formatted string of summary statistics to display under each graph,\n",
    "- errors, the height of half an error bar (ie the error bar for the first data point should be drawn between:\n",
    "   y = y_data[0] - errors[0] and y = y_data[0] + errors[0]\n",
    "- (a and b) are the coefficients of the best-fit line: y = a + b * log(x), where log is the natural log. \n",
    "- You can plot this on the normal graph\n",
    "- And you can also plot y = a + b * x on the graph with a logged x-axis.\n",
    "- residuals - you can plot these in a scatter plot / separate graph below each graph.\n",
    "They give an indicator as to how well the regression line fits the data. Just do N or logN (from x_data on the x axis) and residuals on the y.\n",
    "\n",
    "If you like, change the code in the cell above to make the data match the format you need it in\n",
    "(The title of the graphs might be a bit scuffed as of the moment)\n",
    "\n",
    "I hope this is useful (And sorry if my code is hard to read)\n",
    "'''"
